UID:10004039-1777892400-1777896000@www.unioncong.org
SUMMARY:Women In Palestine Webinar (Offsite and Online)
DESCRIPTION:The Ongoing Nakba and Prospects for Peace and Justice for Palestinians \nFor the past eight decades\, since the establishment of the State of Israel in 1948\, Palestinians have experienced what they call the “ongoing Nakba” (or catastrophe) – displacement and dispossession\, and denial of rights.  Wars and occupation\, expulsion and land appropriation have all been part of what Palestinians have been victims of.  Since 2023\, a genocide in Gaza and intensified military and settler violence in the West Bank\, in addition to the impact of the 2025 and 2026 US and Israeli wars on Iran have shattered Palestinian life and society even more.  In a time when nationalisms are on the rise worldwide\, Israelis and Palestinians both continue to assert national claims and rights on a land inhabited by 7.5 million Israeli Jews and a similar number of Palestinians.  Peace seems as elusive as ever.  What is the state of the quest for peace and justice there today\, after 2½ years of a devastating war and decades of false starts?  What solutions are possible to address the injustices that prevail? \n“Kairos II: Faith in a Time of Genocide\,” with the authors of the Kairos II document\, Rifat Kassis\, General Coordinator of Kairos Palestine\, and Rev. Dr. Munther Isaac\, pastor of Evangelical Lutheran Church of Hope in Ramallah\, Palestine\, is now scheduled for Monday\, May 4 from 11:00 am to 12:00 noon EDT\, with online registration and an opportunity to RSVP to join an in-person watch party and luncheon in Rutherford (RSVP the pastor\, Rev. Annie Allen.  A key theological concept from the document\, published November 2025\, is costly solidarity\, a corollary of Dietrich Bonhoeffer’s costly grace.
URL:https://www.unioncong.org/event/women-in-palestine-webinar-offsite-and-online-2/
LOCATION:Offsite and Online
CATEGORIES:All Church Events,All Events
ORGANIZER;CN="Global Ministries":MAILTO:GlobalMinistriesWeb@ucc.org
END:VEVENT
